  "title": "CHAPTER 15: FOOD & ITS COMPONENTS",
  "order": 16,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "hnpz78d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction to Food & Nutrients"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Carbohydrates and fats are the main energy-yielding nutrients, with fats providing more than twice the energy per gram than carbohydrates.",
        "Proteins act as body-building components essential for growth, repair, and tissue maintenance.",
        "Vitamins and minerals serve as protective nutrients necessary in micro-quantities for regulatory and metabolic functions.",
        "A balanced diet supplies carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals, roughage, and water in proper proportions.",
        "Malnutrition includes undernutrition resulting in protein-energy malnutrition diseases like Kwashiorkor and Marasmus."
      ],
      "id": "mbar5oq"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Major Nutrients",
          "value": "5 Classes",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Fat Energy Yield",
          "value": "9 kcal/g",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Carb/Protein Yield",
          "value": "4 kcal/g",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Core Target",
          "value": "Balanced Diet",
          "icon": "info"
        }
      ],
      "id": "eqd3z2x"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rb2g4s5",
      "content": "Food provides energy, growth materials and regulatory substances required for proper functioning of the body. The major components of food include carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins and minerals."
    },
    {
      "id": "av6gdyi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "hvel2kl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Carbohydrates"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x7ogj5y",
      "content": "Carbohydrates are the primary source of energy. They are composed of carbon, hydrogen and oxygen."
    },
