    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "01lybuo",
      "content": "1. Roughage (dietary fiber) helps in proper bowel movement and prevents constipation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ufo0q6q",
      "content": "2. Water is an essential nutrient that regulates body temperature and transports nutrients."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "itvny64",
      "content": "3. Glycogen is the storage form of carbohydrates in animals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2eiwjaq",
      "content": "4. Essential amino acids cannot be synthesized by the body and must be obtained from diet."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zlook4f",
      "content": "5. Omega-3 fatty acids are beneficial for heart health."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c6wkpe8",
      "content": "6. Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) is the minimum energy required at rest."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "60wxkko",
      "content": "7. BMI (Body Mass Index) is used to assess underweight and obesity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pnnr3ij",
      "content": "8. Overnutrition can lead to obesity, diabetes and cardiovascular diseases."
    },
    {
